<ArticleLayout slug="consumer-electronics-launch-content" ctaLabel="Plan a launch build" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">Consumer electronics product launch content is an asset list with an accuracy layer on top. That layer covers screens, certification marks, claimed specs and energy labels, and it decides which assets can be generated and which have to be shot on the real device.</p>

  <h2>What does consumer electronics product launch content include?</h2>

  <p>A consumer electronics launch needs a hero film and its cut-downs, a marketplace listing set, product and packaging stills, interface renders, and the certification mark and energy label images the rules call for. Each one shows a device making claims. hubStudio builds the list against those rules first, because they decide what can be generated.</p>

  <p>The pages that rank for this topic list assets and stop there.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Across four buyer phrasings and 32 search results, one page came from a regulator, and it was a 2018 proposal to repeal a 1966 rule on stating TV screen size. None of the six results read in full addressed certification marks, energy labels or a ruling on product imagery.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: search-results audit run 10 September 2026 across four buyer phrasings, publisher type recorded for every result.</p>

  <p>So the list below comes with the accuracy check attached. The second and third columns are production practice on every row. They describe what a reviewer checks, not what a rule prescribes.</p>

